{"id":"u-c49fb416-19d2-4378-b48d-62fdd22914dc","src":"community","title":"Tactical Barbell - Mass Protocol - Grey Man","author":"Krisly en Jonathan","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/uHUdSh-grey-man","desc":"- Focus on compound lifts: Bench Press, Deadlift, (High Bar due to personal preference) Squat, Military Press\n\n- Percentage-based programming for compounds (as written). Add 2.5kg for Bench & Press, 5kg for Squat and Deadlift at the end of the program and run it back, repeat.\n\n- Bench & Squat are done together, this is Alpha day. Press & Deadlift are also done together, this is Bravo day\n\n- Accessories are structured in two sets. Both to failure, if 12 reps are reached on both sets, up the weight next time. \n\n- The accessory selection has been inspired by 5/3/1. Meaning Alpha has 1 push, 1 pull, and 1 leg exercise. Same for Bravo but a different group of exercises. These remain the same for progression purposes.\n\n- Abs/Core can be implemented at the end of every workout. Cable crunch or hanging leg raises are recommended.\n\n- Do your cardio. Runs, cycling, rowing,… Do them on your off days and/or schedule them in an AM/PM fashion.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":54,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-30T17:11:35.533Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Alpha","Bravo","Alpha"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"High Bar Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Single Leg Deadlift","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":10,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Neutral Grip, Weighted)","sets":[{"